---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AuthorBio from '../../components/AuthorBio.astro';
import { sections, totalCount } from '../../data/resources';
---

<Layout title="About - AllTheFreeStock" description="Who curates AllTheFreeStock and why the directory exists.">
  <main class="max-w-[720px] mx-auto px-5 pt-20 pb-24">
    <h1 class="font-serif font-normal text-[clamp(38px,5.4vw,56px)] tracking-tight m-0">About</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#4a5c56]">
      AllTheFreeStock is a hand-curated directory of free photos, video, audio, icons, fonts, mockups and
      templates - started in 2015 as a personal bookmarks list that got out of hand.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 flex gap-6 flex-wrap font-mono text-xs text-[#56685f]">
      <span>{totalCount} resources</span>
      <span>{sections.length} categories</span>
      <span>curated since 2015</span>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[#26332f]">
      <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[26px] tracking-tight mt-2 mb-0">Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        "Free" stock sites come and go, change their terms, or quietly get bought and repurposed. This directory
        exists so that list stays useful: every link is checked, dead or hijacked ones get removed, and each entry
        carries a plain-language licence tag instead of leaving you to dig through terms pages.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[26px] tracking-tight mt-4 mb-0">How entries get added</h2>
      <p>
        Most of the directory comes from things I've used in client and personal work over the years. Anyone can
        also <a href="/submit/">submit a resource</a> - submissions are reviewed by hand before they go live, and
        anything without a genuinely free tier is marked with a paid pill rather than left ambiguous.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[26px] tracking-tight mt-4 mb-0">The Journal</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/blog/">blog</a> covers the parts of "free" that trip people up in practice - licensing,
        sourcing, and the workflow habits that keep a project out of trouble.
      </p>
    </div>

    <AuthorBio />
  </main>
</Layout>
